<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11796v1/qa_new.png" id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/188;" width="476" height="188" alt="Refer to caption">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>. </span><span id="S5.F3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Statistics of Gym-QA (<span id="S5.F3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">left</span>) and Diving-QA (<span id="S5.F3.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">right</span>). The total number of Gym-QA QA pairs is <math id="S5.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27,469" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>27,469</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27,469</annotation></semantics></math>; Diving-QA totaled <math id="S5.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,055" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,055</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,055</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">❷<span id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relational Scene Level.</span> To address ambiguities at the instance level, we model relationships within the visual scene graph of <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{i}_{n}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐢</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{i}_{n}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, the relational triple {"athlete", "on top", "balance beam"} is formatted as <span id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"The athlete on top of the balance beam"</span>. Notably, we further design a <span id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">negative</span> format, <span id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"The athlete <span id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> on top of the balance beam"</span>, , to emphasize relational clarity. The visual-to-relation (V2R) similarity is calculated as:</p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sim_{V2R}^{pos}=\frac{\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\cdot\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{pos}}{\left\|\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\right\|\left\|\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{pos}\right\|},\quad sim_{V2R}^{neg}=\frac{\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\cdot\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{neg}}{\left\|\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\right\|\left\|\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{neg}\right\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sim_{V2R}^{pos}=\frac{\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\cdot\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{pos}}{\left\|\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\right\|\left\|\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{pos}\right\|},\quad sim_{V2R}^{neg}=\frac{\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\cdot\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{neg}}{\left\|\hat{\mathcal{C}}[j]\right\|\left\|\mathbf{r}_{n_{id}}^{neg}\right\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the final V2R similarity is defined as: <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sim_{V2R}=sim_{V2R}^{pos}-sim_{V2R}^{neg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sim_{V2R}=sim_{V2R}^{pos}-sim_{V2R}^{neg}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By integrating the instance-level and relational-level matching, we select the terminologies and descriptions of the <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> most similar action types from SSGraph <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{SS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{SS}</annotation></semantics></math> and incorporate them into the reasoning prompt <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> to enrich the knowledge base.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The enriched reasoning prompt <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p_{r}}=\mathcal{S}_{match}(p_{r},\hat{\mathcal{C}},\mathbf{C},\mathcal{G}_{SS})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p_{r}}=\mathcal{S}_{match}(p_{r},\hat{\mathcal{C}},\mathbf{C},\mathcal{G}_{SS})</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the captions <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and input query <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, is passed to the LLM reasoner <math id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{Reason}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{Reason}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> for zero-shot sports VideoQA:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSSx3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Answer}=\mathcal{P}_{Reason}(\mathcal{E}_{V}(\mathcal{Q}),\mathcal{E}_{L}(\hat{\mathcal{C}},\hat{p_{r}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Answer</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Answer}=\mathcal{P}_{Reason}(\mathcal{E}_{V}(\mathcal{Q}),\mathcal{E}_{L}(\hat{\mathcal{C}},\hat{p_{r}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Benchmarking High-speed Sports: Gym-QA &amp; Diving-QA</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Constructing video understanding datasets, particularly for sports videos, poses significant challenges in terms of video collection and annotation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mangalam et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Existing benchmarks like Sports-QA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> provide limited query depth and diversity, while SPORTU <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al., 2024</a>)</cite> focuses on slow-motion clips. To address these limitations, we introduce two high-quality benchmarks, <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gym-QA</span> and <span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diving-QA</span>, tailored for high-speed sports VideoQA. These benchmarks are constructed using FineGym <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2020a</a>)</cite> and FineDiving <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, with systematically designed QA pairs categorized into three difficulty levels (examples can be found in Fig.<span id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;"> <a href="#S7.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 7.3. Ablation Studies ‣ 7. Experiment ‣ FineQuest: Adaptive Knowledge-Assisted Sports Video Understanding via Agent-of-Thoughts Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></span>(a)): <span id="S6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Easy</span>, <span id="S6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Medium</span>, and <span id="S6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hard</span>.
Additionally, we propose a novel <span id="S6.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Action Subset</span>, designed to evaluate the comprehension of intricate visual details in sports, further divided into three coarse-to-fine levels: <span id="S6.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Event</span>, <span id="S6.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Set</span>, and <span id="S6.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Element</span>.
An overview of benchmark statistics is shown in Fig.<span id="S6.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;"> <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Fine-grained Matcher. ‣ 5.2. Deliberative Mode ‣ 5. Methodology ‣ FineQuest: Adaptive Knowledge-Assisted Sports Video Understanding via Agent-of-Thoughts Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>. For detailed construction processes and examples, please refer to <span id="S6.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix</span> §<span id="S6.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;">C</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>. </span><span id="S6.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study of components of FineQuest on the full set of Gym-QA and Diving-QA.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S6.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S6.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Methods</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Easy<math id="S6.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Med.<math id="S6.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hard<math id="S6.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Over.<math id="S6.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T3.5.2" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">
<td id="S6.T3.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">FineQuest</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">80.1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">50.0</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">47.9</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6FFFF;">57.0</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T3.5.3" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">
<td id="S6.T3.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">w/o <math id="S6.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\text{React}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathbackground="#FFFFE6">ℱ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;" mathbackground="#FFFFE6">React</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\text{React}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">78.8</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">50.0</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">48.1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T3.5.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:3pt 2.3pt;"><span id="S6.T3.5.3.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">56.7</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T3.5.4" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFE6;">
