<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitation and Future Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While FineQuest excels at unlocking the sports video understanding capabilities of multimodal large language models, there remains room for exploration in its broader applications, such as sports commentary and acting as a judge or referee in sports scenarios. Additionally, enhancing its domain-specific knowledge base and incorporating more sophisticated reasoning mechanisms could allow FineQuest to better understand and interpret complex sports scenarios, making it a valuable tool for broadcasters and sports analysts alike.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Details of Dynamic Motion Segmenter</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide detailed pseudocode for the Dynamic Motion Segmenter algorithm. This algorithm is a crucial component of our system, designed to accurately segment and analyze motion within sports videos. The pseudocode outlines the step-by-step process used to identify and segment dynamic motions, ensuring precise analysis and understanding of complex sports actions. This detailed breakdown will aid in replicating or adapting the segmenter for various applications within sports video analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{algorithm}</span>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[h]
<span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_caption">Dynamic Motion Segmenter</span>
<span id="A2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{algorithmic}</span>[1]
<span id="A2.p2.2.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><span id="A2.p2.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require:</span> <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>: SAM 2 masked video; <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="win\_size" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">win\_size</annotation></semantics></math>: initial window size; <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\_range" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\_range</annotation></semantics></math>: range for z-score; <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="clip\_len" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">clip\_len</annotation></semantics></math>: range for minimum clip length</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Function</span>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{segment}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{segment}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="motions\leftarrow\text{GetMotions}(\hat{\mathcal{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>GetMotions</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">motions\leftarrow\text{GetMotions}(\hat{\mathcal{V}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Comment</span>Using optical flow
<span id="A2.p3.2.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="proposals\leftarrow[{\color[rgb]{1,1,1}1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">proposals\leftarrow[{\color[rgb]{1,1,1}1}]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p3.2.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Comment</span>Initialize proposal list
<span id="A2.p3.2.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="win\_size\leftarrow win\_size" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">win\_size\leftarrow win\_size</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\For</span>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{win\_size,\ldots,|motions|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{win\_size,\ldots,|motions|\}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="window\leftarrow\text{motions}[i-win\_size:i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext>motions</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">window\leftarrow\text{motions}[i-win\_size:i]</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p4.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mean\leftarrow\text{mean}(window)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mean\leftarrow\text{mean}(window)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p4.2.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="std\leftarrow\text{std}(window)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">std\leftarrow\text{std}(window)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p4.2.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leftarrow\text{adjust based on variability within }z\_range" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>adjust based on variability within </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leftarrow\text{adjust based on variability within }z\_range</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p4.2.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="threshold\leftarrow mean-z\times std" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">threshold\leftarrow mean-z\times std</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\If</span>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{motions}[i]&lt;threshold" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>motions</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{motions}[i]&lt;threshold</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-\text{last\_b}\geq\text{adjusted clip\_len}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mtext>last_b</mtext></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mtext>adjusted clip_len</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-\text{last\_b}\geq\text{adjusted clip\_len}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p5.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="proposals\text{.append}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.append</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">proposals\text{.append}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p5.2.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Comment</span>Add new proposal
<span id="A2.p5.2.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\EndIf</span><span id="A2.p5.2.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\EndFor</span><span id="A2.p5.2.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><span id="A2.p5.2.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Return</span><math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="proposals" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">proposals</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p5.2.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\EndFunction</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para"><span id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Function</span>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{GetMotions}(\hat{\mathcal{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>GetMotions</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{GetMotions}(\hat{\mathcal{V}})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="motions\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">motions\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\For</span><math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\ldots,|\hat{\mathcal{V}}|-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\ldots,|\hat{\mathcal{V}}|-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="frame\_t\leftarrow\hat{\mathcal{V}}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">frame\_t\leftarrow\hat{\mathcal{V}}[t]</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="frame\_t+1\leftarrow\hat{\mathcal{V}}[t+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">frame\_t+1\leftarrow\hat{\mathcal{V}}[t+1]</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="flow\leftarrow\text{OptFlow}(frame\_t,frame\_t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>OptFlow</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">flow\leftarrow\text{OptFlow}(frame\_t,frame\_t+1)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="motion\leftarrow\text{AggFlow}(flow)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>AggFlow</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">motion\leftarrow\text{AggFlow}(flow)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p6.2.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Comment</span>e.g., magnitude, direction
<span id="A2.p6.2.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><math id="A2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="motions\text{.append}(motion)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.append</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">motions\text{.append}(motion)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.9" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\EndFor</span><span id="A2.p6.2.10" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\State</span><span id="A2.p6.2.11" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\Return</span><math id="A2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="motions" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">motions</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="A2.p6.2.12" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\EndFunction</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Details of Gym-QA &amp; Diving-QA</h2>

<section id="A3.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">Raw Data Collection.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FineGym <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2020a</a>)</cite> and FineDiving <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> are two high-quality, fine-grained video datasets originally designed for action understanding tasks such as recognition and quality assessment. These datasets feature hierarchical annotations at multiple semantic levels and consist of high-resolution (<span id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, 720P and 1080P) official video recordings, ensuring completeness and visual clarity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To adapt these datasets for VideoQA, we segmented FineGym into <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6,031" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6,031</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6,031</annotation></semantics></math> event-level clips, each containing <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> element actions, while for FineDiving, we collected videos corresponding to its <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="31" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>31</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">31</annotation></semantics></math> action types, each encompassing <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSSx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> sub-actions. These adaptations ensure sufficient diversity and complexity, laying a solid foundation for constructing challenging QA tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">Question Answer Generation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Different from existing works (<span id="A3.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, EgoSchema <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mangalam et al., 2024</a>)</cite>) that rely on LLMs for QA generation, the subtle visual differences and domain-specific knowledge in sports videos demand a more rigorous approach. We employed a human-centric annotation process with the following key steps: ① Annotators underwent rigorous training to ensure familiarity with the annotation guidelines. ② Question generation and answer annotation were performed in separate stages to maintain objectivity, with invalid questions being refined or discarded. ③ Questions were designed to be answerable solely by watching the video, avoiding reliance on general knowledge.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">Multi-choice Generation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To enhance the QA format, open-ended questions were converted to multiple-choice questions. Using GPT-4o(mni) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2024</a>)</cite>, we generated three distractor options for each question, ensuring they were semantically coherent, unique, and distinct from the correct answer. Additionally, we introduced a novel category of <span id="A3.SS0.SSSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Action Subset</span>, specifically targeting fine-grained action recognition, which directly evaluates a model’s ability to comprehend intricate visual details in sports.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">Query Difficulty Classification.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Full set, we categorized questions into three difficulty levels:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Easy</span>: Requires only a coarse understanding of the video.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Medium</span>: Demands a more fine-grained comprehension of the content.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hard</span>: Involves domain-specific sports knowledge, challenging the model’s ability to understand specialized content.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the Action set, we further classified questions based on the action category into three levels:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Event</span>: Pertains to broader actions or sequences within the sport.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set</span>: Focuses on more specific segments or routines.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Element</span>: Targets the finest details and individual movements, requiring precise recognition and understanding of intricate visual details.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This structured approach ensures a comprehensive assessment of a model’s capability to understand and analyze sports videos at varying levels of complexity and detail.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSSx5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">QA Examination and Filtering.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSSx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSSx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the quality of Gym-QA and Diving-QA, we implemented a multi-stage filtering pipeline: ❶ <span id="A3.SS0.SSSx5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rule-based filtering</span>: Pre-configured filters and NLTK tools<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            https://github.com/nltk/nltk</span></span></span> were used to clean noise and correct grammatical errors. ❷ <span id="A3.SS0.SSSx5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM-based blind filtering</span>: GPT-4o was used to predict answers based solely on the question text, ensuring that questions were grounded in video content. ❸ <span id="A3.SS0.SSSx5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human examination</span>: Each QA pair, along with its corresponding video, was manually inspected based on our SSGraph to verify accuracy and relevance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Extended Details of Methodology: Prompts</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our deployment, we implement an MLLM to act as the reactive reasoning agent. This agent is responsible for executing a structured reasoning process that follows two main stages: <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Query Difficulty Analysis</span> and <span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decision Making</span>. The instruction prompt for this operation is as follows:</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.fig1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11796v1/prompt.svg" id="A4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/842;" width="476" height="842"></object>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>More Experimental Analysis</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents additional experimental analysis. It includes the hierarchical contrastive decoding of the Key Clip Selector and Hyperparameters of FineQuest.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1. </span>Analysis of Key Clip Selector</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the impact of the hierarchical contrastive decoding strategy across three dimensions: ➀ Spatial, ➁ Temporal, and ➂ Spatio-Temporal. The results, as shown in Table<span id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;"> <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ E.1. Analysis of Key Clip Selector ‣ Appendix E More Experimental Analysis ‣ FineQuest: Adaptive Knowledge-Assisted Sports Video Understanding via Agent-of-Thoughts Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></span>, demonstrate that each dimension of distortion significantly influences the Key Clip Selector’s choices. This further validates the effectiveness of employing a multidimensional contrastive strategy when considering videos.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T5.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T5.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 3.4pt;"><span id="A5.T5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spatial</span></td>
<td id="A5.T5.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 3.4pt;"><span id="A5.T5.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temporal</span></td>
<td id="A5.T5.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 3.4pt;"><span id="A5.T5.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spa&amp;Tem</span></td>
<td id="A5.T5.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:3pt 3.4pt;"><span id="A5.T5.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Easy<math id="A5.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
